WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:06.089
Hey this is Presh Talwalkar. This problem
has been shared millions of times on

00:00:06.089 --> 00:00:13.049
Facebook and Twitter with the claim that
99% failed to solve it, and that only a

00:00:13.049 --> 00:00:18.840
genius could find the correct answer. In
this video I'm going to explain what

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:24.220
many people believe to be the correct
answer. Can you figure it out?

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:31.440
Give this problem a try. And when you're ready, keep watching the video for the solution.

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:39.380
So most people believe the correct answer is 6.

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:47.500
The pattern is to take the number on the left hand side of the equation and multiply it by 1 less than itself.

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:56.120
For example the first line would read 9
times 8 which equals 72.

00:00:56.580 --> 00:01:05.780
The next line would be 8 times 7 which equals 56. We then have 7 times 6 which equals 42.

00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:12.640
6 times 5 which equals 30. 5 times 4 which equals 20. And finally we would have 3

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:15.100
times 2 which equals 6.

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:21.120
But not everyone believes 6 is the correct answer.

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:25.220
Some people argue the correct answer is 12.

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:32.880
They identify a pattern of decreasing subtraction in the number on the right hand side.

00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:49.180
So let's see how this pattern works. We start out with 9 equals 72. To get to the next line we subtract by 16 to get to 56. So that is why 8 equals 56.

00:01:49.189 --> 00:01:55.560
Now how do we get to the next line?
Rather than subtracting by 16 they would

00:01:55.560 --> 00:02:00.540
say you should decrease the amount
you're subtracting by to be 14. So then

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:09.239
we have 56 minus 14 equals 42. This gives us the next line of 7 equals 42. We now

00:02:09.239 --> 00:02:13.709
subtract by 2 less so we have 42 minus
12 which equals 30.

00:02:13.709 --> 00:02:19.349
And that gets us to the next line. We
then subtract by two less again so we

00:02:19.349 --> 00:02:25.439
have 30 minus 10 which equals 20. So we
have 5 equals 20 and then we want to

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:31.580
subtract by 2 less which will be 8. And
that will be 20 minus 8 which equals 12.

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:36.560
And that's why they argue the answer is 3 equals 12.

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:38.860
But hold on!

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:46.580
There's a third group of people who say the answer is neither 6 nor 12 but actually that the answer is 9.

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:52.840
Their method is looking at a pattern of decreasing multiplication.

00:02:53.480 --> 00:03:00.020
So this is very much like the answer being 6. You multiply a number by one less than itself.

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:04.469
The difference in this method is now
they say look at the numbers you're

00:03:04.469 --> 00:03:11.360
multiplying by. This is a sequence of
numbers. We have 8, 7, 6, 5, and 4.

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:16.620
So this group of people argues that
if you decrease this you would get the

00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:21.359
next line, which means you should
multiply the next line by 3. So they

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:27.300
would say the answer is 3 times
3 which equals 9.

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:34.580
So now let's recap the three different answers. Some people say the answer is 6; other

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:40.580
people say the answer is 12; and even
other people say the answer is 9.

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:48.420
Now it's a common question which of these answers is correct. Is there a more correct answer than any of the others?

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:53.280
Well from the information we're given in the puzzle we can't definitively say.

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:56.729
But what we can do is we can ask: is any of

00:03:56.780 --> 00:04:01.560
these answers is justifiable under the
patterns of the given methods?

00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:08.040
And by that standard, the answer of 6 is
justifiable by the two other methods.

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:13.300
We can actually reconcile this to show that 6 is a very reasonable answer.

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:20.060
How can we do that? Let's start out with the logic of the decreasing subtraction.

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:27.500
So here's the information of the pattern.
Each time you're subtracting by 2 less than before.

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:31.500
So now the question is: is there, or are

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:36.090
there any other patterns, in this? Well
what you can do is focus on the first

00:04:36.090 --> 00:04:42.940
number in each line. We have a sequence
here. We have 9, 8, 7, 6, and 5.

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:48.800
By this logic--that we should have a
sequence--we should then have a sequence

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:54.500
that the next line be 1 less than 5.
So the next line should be 4.

00:04:54.940 --> 00:05:02.120
And by the logic of decreasing subtraction we would then have 4 equals 12.

00:05:02.120 --> 00:05:06.220
So then how do we figure out what the next line is? How do we get to what 3 equals?

00:05:06.220 --> 00:05:09.680
Well we look at the numbers we're
subtracting by.

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:15.600
If we have this logic of decreasing subtraction we should subtract by 2 less than 8 so that

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:22.500
means the next line would have 12 minus
6. And that would give us the answer on

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:27.750
the right-hand side of the next line
which equals 6. So if we decrease 4 we

00:05:27.750 --> 00:05:32.220
then have the next line being 3 and then
we have the answer of 6 by this

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:38.160
decreasing subtraction method. So once
again we figured out that 3 equals 6 and

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:43.060
the answer is 6 by the very same
decreasing subtraction method.

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:50.160
The only thing we had to do is we had to add the missing line of 4 equals 12.

00:05:51.500 --> 00:05:56.920
We can use the same kind of logic for the
decreasing multiplication method.

00:05:57.820 --> 00:06:04.060
Here's the information from the pattern which they argue about the decreasing multiplication method.

00:06:04.360 --> 00:06:08.720
So we're supposed to be looking for a logic to this--these numbers.

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:13.740
But what we can do--is--we can
look at the first number in every single line.

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:20.120
We have a sequence here of numbers
9, 8, 7, 6, and 5. So logic would suggest the

00:06:20.120 --> 00:06:23.760
next line should start out with 4.

00:06:25.140 --> 00:06:31.600
We then look at the numbers that we are multiplying by and that's another sequence 8, 7, 6, 5, &amp; 4.

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:35.980
So logic would suggest the next line should be multiplied by 3.

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:40.540
So the next line should be 4 multiplied by 3 equals 12.

00:06:41.220 --> 00:06:42.980
If we continue this pattern the first

00:06:43.100 --> 00:06:47.480
number will be one less and the second
number will be one less so the next line

00:06:47.480 --> 00:06:53.900
would be 3 times 2. And once again
3 times 2 equals 6.

00:06:54.460 --> 00:06:57.920
So we again have the answer being equal to 6.

00:06:58.380 --> 00:07:04.880
This is even true under the decreasing multiplication method as long as we include the missing line of 4 times 3 equals 12.

00:07:07.880 --> 00:07:12.540
So to recap: it doesn't matter which method we're using.

00:07:12.920 --> 00:07:20.820
We're always going to get to the answer that 3 equals 6. And in fact we would have 4 equals 12 in each of these methods too.

00:07:21.400 --> 00:07:28.640
So this logic would suggest that the correct answer to this puzzle is that 3 equals 6.

